#version 450
// Port of zwwm's island-mask.comp (from ShojiWM's island-mask, MIT, bea4dev).
// R is coverage, G the alpha itself. zwwm takes the window's alpha; here the
// shape is the rectangle's own rounded outline.
//
// @vw name: Island mask
// @vw params: surface_opacity
#define VW_USE_TARGETS
#include <vw/shader.glsl>

void main() {
  ivec2 pixel;
  if (!vw_pass_begin(pixel)) return;
  vec2 local = vw_pass_local(pixel);
  float clip = clamp(0.5 - vw_rounded_box(local - vw_size() * 0.5, vw_size() * 0.5, vw_radius()), 0.0, 1.0);
  float alpha = clip;
  // Coverage is alpha over the surface's own opacity, so a translucent surface still counts as solid glass.
  float coverage = clamp(alpha / max(vw_param(0), 0.0001), 0.0, 1.0);
  vw_store(pixel, vec4(coverage, alpha, 0.0, 1.0));
}
